          ]
        },
        {
          "section": null,
          "text": "The two-year Child Development Program leads to an associate of arts degree as described:",
          "codes": []
        },
        {
          "section": null,
          "text": "The above program leads to an associate of arts degree in child development. It may be integrated into Franciscan University of Steubenville’s four-year Bachelor of Science degree program in primary education. Upon successful completion of application to the Teacher Education Program as an education (Pre-K-5) major, the student then qualifies for state licensure in teaching at the Pre-K through fifth grade level.",
